 Implementation details\\n\\n- Intercept `Ctrl+Enter` and `Meta+Enter` during capture, before MDXEditor handles the key.\\n- Prevent default behavior and stop propagation, then flush the latest prompt before running the existing shortcut callback.\\n- Keep plain `Enter`, `Shift+Enter`, and disabled shortcut behavior unchanged.\\n- Extend `action_agent_prompt.test.tsx` with regression coverage proving the editor does not receive the send shortcut.\\n\\n# Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- `Ctrl+Enter` sends current prompt without inserting a newline.\\n- `Meta+Enter` has same behavior.\\n- Prompt is flushed before send callback runs.\\n- Plain `Enter` and `Shift+Enter` still insert newlines.\\n\\r\\n\",\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:30:- Remove `useActionPopupController`; do not replace it with another aggregate controller.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:62:- [ ] `useActionPopupController` is deleted.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_023_use_one_agent_conversation_model.md:27:J-020 unified conversation content into `entries`, but renderer run state still stores `LiveAgentTurn`. `useActionPopupController` converts that object into a new `AgentConversation` during rendering. This duplicates models, metadata, and ownership.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:31:- `useActionPopupController` stores prompt value, preparation status, and reset token in React state.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:59:- `useActionPopupController` removes `promptState`, `promptResetToken`, prompt-value derivation, and `handlePromptChange` state updates.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_021_derive_markdown_styles_globally.md:31:`AppThemeProvider` owns `markdownStyleConfig`, but consumers receive only the raw configuration. Both `MarkdownEditor` and `ActionConversationChat` call `buildMarkdownContentSx(markdownStyleConfig)` in their render bodies. The builder crea